        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. King Charles III lays out UK government agenda as Starmer's job hangs in the balance Issued on: 13/05/2026 - 15:25 King Charles III laid out on Wednesday the British government’s legislative program for the coming year or so, as Prime Minister Keir Starmer fought to remain in power following rising discontent within his Labour Party. In a speech to lawmakers laced with all the pomp that accompanies the ceremonial opening of Parliament, the king said the U.K.'s energy policy, defense and national security would be tested as it deals with the fallout from the wars in Iran and Ukraine. FRANCE 24's Bénédicte Paviot reports from London. Xi-Trump summit: The humble soybean at the heart of a trade dispute between the US and China 13/05/2026 Fabled Argentine city Ushuaia tries to shrug off hantavirus suspicions 13/05/2026 REPLAY: King Charles lays out Starmer's agenda as PM fights for survival 13/05/2026 French woman battling 'severe' hantavirus as outbreak grows to 11 13/05/2026 Sarkozy appeal trial: Prosecution wrapping case ahead of sentencing request 13/05/2026 Who walks the red carpet at Cannes? 13/05/2026 Culture Hantavirus: US cruiseship passenger gives quarantine room tour 13/05/2026 Americas Israel and favorite Finland advance to the Eurovision final 13/05/2026 Ahead of Trump-Xi summit, China warns on US arms sales to Taiwan 13/05/2026"
